From 0cb88b94b870466f54bd7de8a8c7c404b4529518 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan <nathan@nr5p.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:31:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Modem core from upstream xara 0.1.2 and 0.1.3: FM timing,
 speedups

Applies upstream's changes to xara-arq and xara-phy; with this the two
crates match upstream 0.1.3 apart from this fork's own BUSY noise-shape
fix and registered-level modulation names.

- FM reply windows are taken from the last 8 exchanges instead of the
  whole session, and widen by 38 ticks per missed reply (up to 4), so a
  window left behind by drifting reply times catches up instead of
  stalling the link (x0rro/xara#20)
- sine tables, a shared FFT plan, in-place FFTs and a parallel FM OFDM
  catch-up search; quantise without round_ties_even, tested bit-identical
- warm() for the HF and FM tables, so the first frame doesn't pay for them
