From 3838b398d012b1ab6af4808d1d86c857670c0855 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan <nathan@nr5p.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:31:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Allow for the PTT tail in the reply window (from upstream
 xara 0.1.3)

With --ptt-tail-ms the transmitter stays keyed after the audio ends, so
the peer answers that much later; the reply deadline was taken from the
audio end, and on a rig with a 100 ms tail the connect reply arrived
after xara had keyed again (x0rro/xara#28). The tail (none for VOX or
no PTT) now goes to on_tx_done in both HF and FM.

Also from upstream's station code: a burst's trailing silence is carried
as a count rather than appended samples; the scheduler takes an rx_lag
(capture lag) that shortens the PTT hold, left at 0 here since this
fork's backends report their latency as a round trip; and
set_tx_latency. Upstream's tests for these come along, and the
1000 ms-lead FM test now accepts a slow link as well as a stalled one,
as upstream's does, since the timing fix lets it finish.
